{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "cd7bbe88-a4f1-8d1e-af14-8b3e8580ba73",
  "created_at": "2026-01-27T14:49:06-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Finance",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Brendan Hanlon",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Janet Whitcomb",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:46:47-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "City of Newport, Finance Department, this is Janet Whitcomb. How may I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:46:53-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, good afternoon. My name's Brendan Hanlon. I'm calling about a property tax bill for my mother. She's at 234 Kingston Avenue, up on the Hill."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:47:02-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Certainly, Mr. Hanlon. What can I do for you regarding that account?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:47:07-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Two things. First, she needs a duplicate bill mailed. The last one got lost, or she put it somewhere, I couldn't tell you. I tried the website first, but I'd rather just talk to a person, honestly."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:47:20-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's perfectly fine. I can request a duplicate bill for that address. It will go to the mailing address we have on file. Is that the same as the property address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:47:31-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, same. 234 Kingston. She's lived there a long time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:47:35-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "All right. I've put in the request. It should arrive in the mail within several business days."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:47:41-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, good. And the other thing, is there a senior exemption? Or a veteran one? My father was a veteran, but he's gone, and my mother's, she's in her eighties. I don't know if either of those applies."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:47:54-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There are exemption programs for seniors and for veterans, yes. Eligibility depends on the specific requirements, such as age, residency, and in some cases income or service records. Applications are handled through the Assessor's office, not Finance."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:48:07-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So how do I apply? Is there a form?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:48:11-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There is an application. I would suggest you contact the Assessor's office and ask them to send the form and a list of required documents. I can transfer you now if you like."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:48:23-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, please. Wait, before you do, does the exemption come off the bill itself, or do you get money back after?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:48:31-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That is a question for the Assessor's office as well. I would not want to give you incorrect information about how it is applied."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:48:40-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fair enough. Does she have to be the one who applies, or can I do it for her?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:48:47-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The Assessor's staff can tell you who may sign on her behalf. Let me transfer you. If the call drops, they are in the same City Hall system, so you may ask for them directly."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:48:59-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Thanks, Ms. Whitcomb. I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T14:49:02-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Mr. Hanlon. One moment while I connect you."
    }
  ],
